  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"117\" data-end=\"336\">The <strong data-start=\"121\" data-end=\"149\">Cocaine Metabolites Test</strong> is primarily used for <strong data-start=\"172\" data-end=\"204\">detecting recent cocaine use</strong> by identifying its major metabolites&mdash;primarily <strong data-start=\"252\" data-end=\"271\">benzoylecgonine</strong>&mdash;in urine, blood, saliva, or hair. This test is commonly used in:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"338\" data-end=\"501\">\n<li data-start=\"338\" data-end=\"366\">\n<p data-start=\"340\" data-end=\"366\"><strong data-start=\"340\" data-end=\"366\">Workplace drug testing</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"367\" data-end=\"404\">\n<p data-start=\"369\" data-end=\"404\"><strong data-start=\"369\" data-end=\"404\">Clinical toxicology assessments</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"405\" data-end=\"443\">\n<p data-start=\"407\" data-end=\"443\"><strong data-start=\"407\" data-end=\"443\">Legal or forensic investigations</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"444\" data-end=\"501\">\n<p data-start=\"446\" data-end=\"501\"><strong data-start=\"446\" data-end=\"501\">Monitoring patients in drug rehabilitation programs</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"503\" data-end=\"632\">Benzoylecgonine is the primary and most stable metabolite of cocaine and can be detected for a longer period than cocaine itself.</p>\n<p data-start=\"503\" data-end=\"632\">Elevated Levels &ndash; Clinical Implications&nbsp;</p>\n<p data-start=\"503\" data-end=\"632\">A <strong data-start=\"693\" data-end=\"734\">positive test for cocaine metabolites</strong> indicates <strong data-start=\"745\" data-end=\"767\">recent cocaine use</strong>. Time frames for detection vary based on the matrix tested:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Sample Type</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Detection Window</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Urine</strong></td>\n<td>2&ndash;4 days (up to 10 days with chronic use)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Blood</strong></td>\n<td>12&ndash;48 hours</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Saliva</strong></td>\n<td>1&ndash;2 days</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Hair</strong></td>\n<td>Weeks to months (long-term use history)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"503\" data-end=\"632\">&nbsp;</p>",
